{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception-action interface: perception states reflect obstacle sensor outcomes, and action states reflect the execution of motion pulses. The specification binds each perception to a unique safe action, prioritizing forward/random_walk in clear, using short directed turns for side obstacles, and a brief backward escape for front obstacles. Recovery is conservative but brief, always returning to exploration as soon as possible. full_rotate is reserved for rare stuck cases after repeated recovery failures.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception (clear/obstacle) and action (commit/recovery) states in the plant to reflect open-loop pulse semantics and uncontrollable event precedence.",
    "Specification automaton enforces: (1) forward/random_walk in clear, (2) rotate_clockwise for left obstacle, (3) rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacle, (4) move_backward for front obstacle, (5) full_rotate only after repeated stuck, (6) immediate return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
